         <item>
          <widget class="LineEdit" name="txt_output_dir">
           <property name="minimumSize">
            <size>
             <width>0</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="maximumSize">
            <size>
             <width>16777215</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Where the baked lightmaps are written (optional).

Empty — a lightmaps folder in the project's texture folder (sourceimages).
Relative (e.g. 'lightmaps' or 'bake/lm') — resolved under that folder, so the path stays portable across projects.
Absolute (e.g. 'D:/bakes') — used as-is.

The folder is created if it doesn't exist. Browsing to a folder inside the texture folder stores it as a relative path. The image button saves each map beside its material's texture maps instead; this folder then takes only the objects whose material has none.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="placeholderText">
            <string>(blank: sourceimages/lightmaps)</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
         <item>
          <widget class="LineEdit" name="txt000">
           <property name="minimumSize">
            <size>
             <width>0</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="maximumSize">
            <size>
             <width>16777215</width>
             <height>19</height>
            </size>
           </property>
           <property name="toolTip">
            <string>Name affix for the baked lightmap. A leading '_' (e.g. '_Lightmap') is treated as a suffix → &amp;lt;object&amp;gt;_Lightmap; a trailing '_' (e.g. 'LM_') as a prefix. Empty uses the placeholder default.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;The button beside the field cycles Auto / Suffix / Prefix.</string>
           </property>
           <property name="placeholderText">
            <string>_Lightmap</string>
           </property>
          </widget>
         </item>
        </layout>
       </widget>
      </item>
         <item>
          <widget class="QGroupBox" name="grp_process">
           <property name="title">
            <string/>
           </property>
           <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="process_layout">
            <property name="spacing">
             <number>1</number>
            </property>
            <property name="leftMargin">
             <number>2</number>
            </property>
            <property name="topMargin">
             <number>2</number>
            </property>
            <property name="rightMargin">
             <number>2</number>
            </property>
            <property name="bottomMargin">
             <number>2</number>
            </property>
            <item>
             <widget class="ComboBox" name="cmb000">
              <property name="minimumSize">
               <size>
                <width>180</width>
                <height>19</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="maximumSize">
               <size>
                <width>999</width>
                <height>19</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>Preset — this panel's bake settings under a name: Packing, Reflection Probe, Resolution, Samples, GI Samples (Maya), Bounces, Adaptive Sampling, Include Scene Lighting, Include Environment, Include Hidden Lights, Denoise and Beside Material Textures.

      The built-ins (italic, read-only) — preview, mobile, desktop, hero — set the quality dials only. Save (the disk icon) stores the current settings under a name you type (Enter to commit); the ⋯ menu renames, deletes or opens the preset folder. A * after the name means a setting has changed since the preset loaded.

      Not saved: Scope, the Exclude and Isolate sets, Processor, Output Directory and Name — they belong to a scene or a machine. A headless bake reads the same presets: LightmapBaker.from_preset(name).</string>
              </property>
              <property name="frame">
               <bool>false</bool>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
            <item>
             <widget class="QPushButton" name="btn_reset_defaults">
              <property name="minimumSize">
               <size>
                <width>0</width>
                <height>19</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="maximumSize">
               <size>
                <width>16777215</width>
                <height>19</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>Restore every setting on this panel to its default.</string>
              </property>
              <property name="text">
               <string>Reset to Defaults</string>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
            <item>
             <widget class="QPushButton" name="b000">
              <property name="sizePolicy">
               <sizepolicy hsizetype="Preferred" vsizetype="Fixed">
                <horstretch>0</horstretch>
                <verstretch>0</verstretch>
               </sizepolicy>
              </property>
              <property name="minimumSize">
               <size>
                <width>0</width>
                <height>30</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="maximumSize">
               <size>
                <width>16777215</width>
                <height>30</height>
               </size>
              </property>
              <property name="toolTip">
               <string>Bake a lightmap for every object in Scope (minus the Exclude set) and wire it for the engine: pack lightmap UVs, bake white-card lighting into them (Maya: Arnold; Blender: Cycles), dilate the seams, denoise, then record it on the object. The material and its texture UVs are untouched — the engine composites albedo × lightmap.

      Re-baking replaces the previous maps. On the Manage page, right-click a map to Re-Bake or Revert it.</string>
              </property>
              <property name="text">
               <string>Bake Lightmaps</string>
              </property>
             </widget>
            </item>
           </layout>
          </widget>
         </item>
         </layout>
        </widget>
